WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.300
Inside multiply, the block loads left and right tiles into shared memory.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.520
After the barrier, each output thread accumulates products using those tiles.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.270
The second barrier protects tile reuse.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:24.870
Tail loads contribute zero without leaving a barrier; only valid outputs are written. main checks every product element against an independent CPU reference with nonuniform inputs.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.500
Load tiles.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.955
Threads fill shared left and right arrays.

00:00:29.955 --> 00:00:31.575
Reuse operands.

00:00:31.575 --> 00:00:34.665
Several outputs consume the same tile values.

00:00:34.665 --> 00:00:35.970
Protect reuse.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.960
Synchronise before loading the next tiles.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.505
Threads reuse shared tiles while each output sum is working state associated with its thread.

00:00:45.505 --> 00:00:51.415
This multiply kernel uses scalar arithmetic; it does not call matrix-unit instructions.
